/-!
# The dual series as classes of the literal contragredient, admissible for the Stokes lemma

Formalized by Claude Sonnet 5.5.

the `GammaNDual.Hd` / `dualE` (classes of `H²(Γ(N), E^∨)`, `E^∨ = E ∘ ȷ`) transported to the literal contragredient `E_n^*` (`gammaNRepAllDual`) of the Stokes
statement by the equivariant isomorphism `dualIso`:

* `toLiteralG` (bijective), `toLiteralG_res` (commutes with restriction to subgroups), `rep_dual_eq` (the representations agree by `rfl`);
* `HdLit` and `HdLit_zeroFlags`: every literal dual class generated by the dual series has zero restriction to every flag group `Γ(N) ∩ h⁻¹Bh`, which is the hypothesis `hz'` of
  `GammaNStokes.gamma6_stokes_En` (from the `dual_rB_zero`, the `Hd_zeroFlags`);
* `gamma6_stokes_dualSeries`: `gamma6_stokes_En` for the actual dual series at `N = 6`;
* `DualLiteralFaces`: `dualEisenstein_gammaN_literal`, the `dualEisenstein_gammaN` transported to the literal contragredient: `Hd := HdLit`, `QDi i := QDiL i = 𝒞_Q(E*)` (`dualCuspidalQLiteral`), `PD := PDL`, with
  `dualRQL_apply` / `dualRPL_apply` showing that the line and plane coordinates are the `twoCohomologyRestriction (Subgroup.inclusion …)`.

Not proved: the Stokes relation for general `N` (S1/S5 descent from `Γ(lcm(N,6))`) and the identification of the cone face pairings with the algebraic ones.
-/

